    "Heart rate per set — baseline before, peak after" : {
      "comment" : "A label describing the heart rate of a workout.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Heart rate reflects cardiovascular load — reps, time under tension, muscle mass and rest — not how many reps you had left, so RIR here comes from your load against your estimated 1RM. Heart-rate readings are least telling for isolation and upper-body work." : {
      "comment" : "A description of how the heart rate is calculated.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Heart rate rises with heat, caffeine and stress too, and the Watch samples less often outside workouts, so everyday minutes are under-counted." : {
