      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Co to jest"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What it learned from" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Na czym się uczy"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "WHAT MOVED" : {
      "comment" : "A heading for the changes in the user's health metrics.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "WHAT SEEMS TO DRIVE IT" : {
      "comment" : "A heading for the findings that are not strong enough to call.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "What shaped this score" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Co wpłynęło na wynik"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What you ate" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Co zjadłeś"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What you must actually have eaten, worked out backwards from what your body burned and what your weight did. Research teams use this intake-balance method to check food logs without watching people eat." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ile musiałeś faktycznie zjeść, wyliczone wstecz z tego, co organizm spalił i jak zmieniła się waga. Naukowcy używają tej metody, by sprawdzać dzienniki jedzenia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What you'll see" : {
      "comment" : "A label displayed above a list of features that will be available when using a tracker.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "What your body says you ate" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ile zjadłeś według organizmu"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What your daily calories are spent on. When people diet, NEAT — the fidgeting, pacing and everyday movement outside workouts — is often what quietly drops, and it can cancel a large part of a deficit." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Na co idą Twoje dzienne kalorie. Podczas diety często po cichu spada NEAT — codzienny ruch poza treningami — co może zniwelować dużą część deficytu."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What's on the plate" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Co jest na talerzu"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What's the difference between Today, Trends and Analysis?" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Czym różnią się Dziś, Trendy i Analiza?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What's your goal?" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Jaki jest Twój cel?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When Apple Intelligence is on, most of this runs on your iPhone and nothing is sent anywhere. Otherwise aggregated numbers, remaining macros, your dietary notes and photos you choose are sent to Google. Raw Health samples never leave your phone. Recovery, strain and all the analysis maths run on your iPhone without AI." : {
      "comment" : "A description of how the app uses Apple Intelligence.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "When gaining, higher is better — over 50% means mostly lean. When losing, lower is better — under 20% means mostly fat lost with muscle kept." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Przy przybieraniu wyżej znaczy lepiej — ponad 50% to głównie masa beztłuszczowa. Przy chudnięciu niżej znaczy lepiej — poniżej 20% to głównie utrata tłuszczu z zachowaniem mięśni."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where the night went" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Jak minęła noc"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where your calories come from" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Skąd pochodzą Twoje kalorie"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where your calories go" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Na co idą Twoje kalorie"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where your weight is heading if you keep eating like the last two weeks. Unlike the '7,700 kcal = 1 kg forever' rule, it includes the fact that expenditure falls as you lose weight and rises as you gain, so change slows toward a plateau." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dokąd zmierza Twoja waga, jeśli będziesz jeść jak przez ostatnie dwa tygodnie. W przeciwieństwie do reguły „7700 kcal = 1 kg” uwzględnia, że wydatek spada przy chudnięciu i rośnie przy tyciu, więc zmiana zwalnia do plateau."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "WHO 150" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "pl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "WHO 150"
          }
        }
      }
    },
